  "summary": "Jaya Grocer's storefront sites (Shopify-based, per-outlet) were the most productive source, supplying verifiable per-pack MYR pricing for most leafy greens, herbs, fruiting crops, roots and a fresh edible flower (bunga kantan); one item (zucchini) needed a second Jaya Grocer outlet since the primary outlet didn't stock it. Sunway XFarms, a Malaysian urban microgreens farm, supplied pea shoots and white radish microgreens pricing as pre-order harvested boxes. Fresh garden cress and a living/growing microgreen tray could not be located: CityFarm Malaysia only sells microgreen seeds (all sold out, no harvested product), and Lotus's, Village Grocer, AEON/myAEON2go, Cold Storage, Mydin, HappyFresh and GrabMart either required app/location context to show prices or returned no reachable product catalog via fetch."
